{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842242-campaign-help-please","id":842242,"title":"Campaign help, please?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-04T16:47:46-08:00","id":842242,"title":"Campaign help, please?","content":"Alright, so my gaming group is currently planning a Vampire the Masqurade campaign (Wrong forum I know, but bare with me) and I made the comment that if the GM was going to run a oWoD game then I would run a nWoD game. <br /> <br /> That said, I need some help coming up with a campaign that highlights the differences between old and new World of Darkness and also to really bring home the personal horror that World of Darkness is supposed to be based around. Does anyone have some campaign ideas that they could share?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:13:50-08:00","id":842257,"title":"","content":"In my experience more you try to force the differences the game tends to go down hill. After all you are trying to tell a story not sell a system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:43:18-08:00","id":842282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842242-campaign-help-please?p=842257#post842257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience more you try to force the differences the game tends to go down hill. After all you are trying to tell a story not sell a system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. I was going more for like... recurring themes that should be shown. I know the oWoD was about that personal horror, but reading VtR made me think it less about the horror and more about how much of a curse immortality is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:46:05-08:00","id":842286,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, maybe introduce them to a low Humanity Elder to show them what they very well may become if they survive long enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:48:50-08:00","id":842288,"title":"","content":"A lot of the zoomed-in, local level personal horror and individual drama isn't stuff that doesn't <i>happen</i> in Masquerade, simply stuff that is emphasized a little more and, with 2e Requiem, highlighted with mechanics here and there like Touchstones. (The 2e corebook in general is rather more confident about Requiem's distinct identity, having benefitted from years of supplements and different writers exploring and fleshing out that setting.)<br /> <br /> The clanbooks are good. They're packed with little snapshots of interesting stuff you could focus a chronicle around. You'll have to do the heavy lifting, though.<br /> <br /> I'd say one of the tonal differences between Masquerade and Requiem that you <i>could</i> capitalize on is the fact that Requiem more firmly exists in a world where supernatural strangeness is prevalent, unpredictable and poorly understood. Masquerade, especially when played by longtime veterans, tends to have a feel that while vampires' unlives may be complicated by alien monsters with whom they have to share the Earth, those monsters are somewhat defined and even navigable. Ventrue capitalists who deal in a built up Pentex company town are eventually going to learn at least <i>something</i> about banes, Black Spiral Dancers or Pentex First Teams, and if they cross state lines to a neighboring domain, that knowledge will relatively hold. Requiem has more in the way of outside-context problems and miscellaneous strangeness. There's shit in the Chronicles of Darkness that none of the big name gamelines have a firm grip on. Tumorous growths feeding at the bottom of hydroelectric dams. Magical phrases that recur and foresage doom. Lakes that hate. Requiem politics often are thrown bizarre curveballs and then prove themselves by how they adapt to and capitalize on them (or how they fail to do so). If you're short on ideas for the uncanny and bizarre, browse urban legends on Snopes or conspiracy theories and UFO experiences on forum sites like AboveTopSecret. The Chronicles of Darkness take place in a world where some of these are roughly accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:53:08-08:00","id":842292,"title":"","content":"Just emphasizing how the covenants are should help. Don't go with a standard Invictus Prince and choose something more out there, like the Carthian Premier or the Crone Oracle. You could play off the clans, how they are not nearly as tight knight and insular as they were in Masquerade. You could show how a particularly skilled and disciplined neonate or ancilla could easily 'take out' a vampire hundreds and even thousands of years older than them. The Ancient Mysteries book has a number of really old vampires that are comparable to neonates in 'power,' just having a vampire who was around in the days of ancient Egypt but still has the same amount of disciplines and abilities as the players could really show off the difference.<br /> <br /> You also have the strix. And werewolves don't harbor any in-born animosity towards vampires, while some still hunt vampires it's not a given for all werewolves, and some even have vampires in their packs. Offering options for bloodlines might go a long way, too, as they were very different in Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T20:10:35-08:00","id":842372,"title":"","content":"Thank you all, that's going to be a big help. I'd also prefer that this campaign go less like the last one I was part of, where it was kick in the door and stake the bloodsuckers that you didn't like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T20:46:48-08:00","id":842386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dman1123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842242-campaign-help-please?p=842372#post842372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also prefer that this campaign go less like the last one I was part of, where it was kick in the door and stake the bloodsuckers that you didn't like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Combine carrots with sticks.<br /> <br /> The stick is easy: emphasize consequences for the blunt approach, not just in terms of making vampiric enemies but in leaving a trail behind. The police are going to stake you out for attempted murder even if they don't realize you're vulnerable to a literal stake. Put disappearances on the front page of the local paper and watch the kine get skittish and make you work for every meal.<br /> <br /> The carrot is harder but probably more important than the stick. Give them a reason to actively want to spend time peacefully, not just a reason to avoid firefights. Really use those Touchstones. Find out what your players want their characters to value and what they find entertaining and likeable, and give them that, no strings attached. Likeable, funny, helpful NPCs, who aren't there just to be endangered and snatched away... except by the PCs themselves. Never put them in your crosshairs unprovoked, but leave them vulnerable to fallout. &quot;Vulnerable&quot; includes emotionally vulnerable, too: if you manage to endear them to their allies well enough, just the idea that their allies might be shocked or disgusted by certain actions might carry water.<br /> <br /> &quot;Make likeable characters&quot; is easier said than done, more an art than a science. But if you just use the stick, players who like violent solutions aren't going to get more peaceful. They're just going to make sure they're ready to cut a bloody swath out of a crowd for an escape route at a moment's notice.<br /> <br /> More important than all of that, though, is the direct approach: <i>Talk to your players and make explicitly sure they understand that you're hoping for a game where murder isn't the first recourse.</i> Communicate. Make sure they're on board with it before they even make characters. If your players don't want to play along then you can't make them and you'll just make everybody miserable trying. The carrot and the stick are just there to make it easier for them to play along so it goes smoothly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T06:12:44-08:00","id":842510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842242-campaign-help-please?p=842386#post842386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More important than all of that, though, is the direct approach: <i>Talk to your players and make explicitly sure they understand that you're hoping for a game where murder isn't the first recourse.</i> Communicate. Make sure they're on board with it before they even make characters. If your players don't want to play along then you can't make them and you'll just make everybody miserable trying. The carrot and the stick are just there to make it easier for them to play along so it goes smoothly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an important part of most storytelling right there. I'm sure that my players will enjoy being encouraged to be sneaky, once they get past their gut reaction which comes from playing D&amp;D for years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T07:08:52-08:00","id":842542,"title":"","content":"A lot of people feel obliged to put points into combat facesmash stuff because there is certain idea floating around that if you won't, you will get punished and Werewolves/whatever will eat your character. And because it's relatively expensive to become combat monster, it will take up a lot of resources. Which will lead straight into &quot;well, I've spent 60% of my stuff on being able to kill people, I guess my best choice here is to use shit i bought&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T10:54:36-08:00","id":842646,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and so I'll definitely mention that there will be some combat, but it will be very rare. Hopefully that'll help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:13:56-08:00","id":843410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dman1123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842242-campaign-help-please#post842242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so my gaming group is currently planning a Vampire the Masquerade campaign (Wrong forum I know, but bare with me) and I made the comment that if the GM was going to run a oWoD game then I would run a nWoD game.<br /> <br /> That said, I need some help coming up with a campaign that highlights the differences between old and new World of Darkness and also to really bring home the personal horror that World of Darkness is supposed to be based around. Does anyone have some campaign ideas that they could share?</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Elders in Requiem are not that old By Masquerade terms</li> <li>You could start off first tier before moving to second tie- Masq defaults to 2nd tier</li> <li>If you run second tier, look at the alternate styles of domains in second edition</li> <li>Play up blood sympathy.-Masq has nothing like it</li> <li>Run Blood &amp; Smoke rules-2nd edition<ul><li>Use the new sense blood and heartbeat rules</li> <li>Use predators aura</li> <li>2nd edition expands blood sympathy</li> <li>Ghouls are more powerful in requiem in general and more agency in 2nd ed.</li> <li>explain to them that Requiem clans are like meta-clans not unlike the [blank] lineages in noddist lore- requiem bloodlines are closer to masq clans</li> <li>have one of their first kills come back as a revenant</li> <li>Have at least one player posthumously embraced</li> <li>Our disciplines are cooler-especially at first dot</li> <li>play up covenants especially the ones not like a camarilla game (carthian Domain, LS, The Circle, etc)</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}